\subsection{Fluid Dynamics \& DMR Mesh Stress Test}

A synthetic atmospheric shockwave input was applied to the DMR module. Spatial
cells were refined in regions of high vorticity while preserving global mass
and momentum:

\begin{itemize}
  \item \textbf{Continuity Check:}
  \[
  \frac{\partial \rho}{\partial t} + \nabla \cdot (\rho \mathbf{v}) = 0,
  \]
  residual error below machine epsilon
  $\epsilon_m \approx 1.19 \times 10^{-7}$.
  \item \textbf{Harmonic Dampening:}
  Lyapunov functional $V(t)$ decreased monotonically with no spurious
  oscillations, consistent with the proven stability envelope.
\end{itemize}

